<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<script src="/theme-init.js?v=<%= assetVersion %>"></script>
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<title>Terms of Service - <%= siteName %></title>
<meta name="description" content="The terms that govern use of Postfalcon.">
<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/style.css?v=<%= assetVersion %>">
</head>
<body>
<div class="landing dark-canvas">
  <%- include('partials/site-header') %>

  <main class="api-docs">
    <section class="api-docs-hero">
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="landing-subhead">Last updated October 6, 2026</p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Agreement</h2>
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of Postfalcon (postfalcon.co). By creating an account, you agree
        to them. If you don't agree, don't use the service.
      </p>
      <% if (operatorName) { %>
      <p>
        Postfalcon is operated by <%= operatorName %><% if (operatorAbn) { %> (ABN <%= operatorAbn %>)<% } %>, a sole trader based in New South Wales,
        Australia (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;).
      </p>
      <% } %>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        Postfalcon lets you compose, schedule, and cross-post content to social media accounts you
        connect (Mastodon, Bluesky, Facebook, Instagram, Threads, Telegram, YouTube, TikTok,
        Pinterest, LinkedIn, X), via each platform's own API. We are not affiliated with, and do not
        speak for, any of those platforms.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>YouTube</h2>
      <p>
        Postfalcon's YouTube features use YouTube API Services. By connecting a YouTube channel to
        Postfalcon, you agree to be bound by the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/t/terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener">YouTube Terms of Service</a>.
        How Google handles your data is described in the
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>;
        what Postfalcon does with the YouTube data it accesses is covered in our
        <a href="/privacy#youtube">Privacy Policy</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Accounts</h2>
      <p>
        You must be at least 16 years old to use Postfalcon. You're responsible for keeping your
        login credentials and any generated API tokens confidential, and for all activity under your
        account. Tell us right away if you suspect unauthorized access.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Subscription &amp; billing</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Free trial.</strong> Your first subscription starts with a 7-day free trial (one
        trial per customer). We ask for a card when the trial starts. Unless you cancel before the
        trial ends, your subscription begins automatically and the card is charged for your chosen
        plan and billing period on the day the trial ends.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Billing.</strong> Plans are billed in advance, monthly or yearly, in US dollars,
        through our payment processor, Stripe, and <strong>renew automatically</strong> at the end of
        each billing period until cancelled. Prices are shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>.
        If we change a plan's price, the new price applies to new subscriptions; we'll tell you before
        any change to the price of an existing subscription takes effect.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Changes and cancellation.</strong> You can change plan, switch between monthly and
        yearly, update your card, or cancel at any time from <em>Manage billing</em> in Settings.
        Upgrades take effect immediately and are charged pro rata for the rest of the billing period;
        downgrades and a switch from yearly to monthly take effect at the end of the current period.
        Cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period, and you keep access until
        then; we don't provide partial refunds for unused time, except where required by law
        (including the Australian Consumer Law).
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Failed payments.</strong> If a payment fails we'll retry it and email you, and your
        account keeps working while we do. If every retry fails, the subscription is cancelled and
        publishing stops until you subscribe again. Scheduled posts are kept, not deleted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to use Postfalcon to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Post content you don't have the rights to post, or to an account you're not authorized to manage.</li>
        <li>Send spam, or violate the terms of service of any platform you connect through Postfalcon.</li>
        <li>Post unlawful, harassing, or fraudulent content.</li>
        <li>Attempt to disrupt, reverse-engineer, or abuse the service or its API beyond documented rate limits.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        You're responsible for complying with the rules of every platform you connect (Meta, Google,
        TikTok, Pinterest, LinkedIn, Mastodon instances, etc.) — connecting through Postfalcon doesn't
        exempt you from them, and action taken against your account by a third-party platform is
        between you and that platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Your content</h2>
      <p>
        You own whatever you create and post through Postfalcon. By connecting an account and
        scheduling a post, you grant us only the limited permission needed to store, transmit, and
        publish that content to the destinations you choose, on your behalf.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Third-party platforms</h2>
      <p>
        Postfalcon depends on the APIs of the platforms you connect. We aren't responsible for their
        outages, rate limits, policy changes, or account actions — including a connected platform
        revoking access, changing its API, or suspending your account there.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Termination</h2>
      <p>
        You can delete your account at any time from Settings, which removes your account data. We
        may suspend or terminate accounts that violate these terms, including the acceptable-use
        section above.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Disclaimer &amp; limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        Postfalcon is provided "as is," without warranties of any kind. To the extent permitted by
        law, we aren't liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your
        use of the service, including lost posts, missed schedules, or account actions taken by a
        third-party platform.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>If these terms change, we'll update the date at the top of this page.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>These terms are governed by the laws of Australia.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="api-docs-section">
      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these terms? Email <a href="mailto:admin@postfalcon.co">admin@postfalcon.co</a>.</p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="landing-footer">
    <span>&copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> Postfalcon<% if (operatorName) { %> &middot; operated by <%= operatorName %><% if (operatorAbn) { %> (ABN <%= operatorAbn %>)<% } %><% } %></span>
    <% if (blogEnabled) { %><a href="/blog">Blog</a><% } %>
    <a href="/api-docs">API docs</a>
    <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
  </footer>
</div>
<%- include('partials/analytics') %>
</body>
</html>
